{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<pre><code>msgctxt "navigation"
msgid "Home"
msgstr "Startpagina"

msgctxt "address"
msgid "Home"
msgstr "Thuis"</code></pre>
<pre><code>{{"{{"}} ctl .Loc "navigation" "Home" }}
{{"{{"}} ctl .Loc "address" "Home" }}</code></pre>
<p>The pair of context and key identifies an entry. Choose stable contexts describing the meaning of the text. A lookup without a context uses a different entry.</p>
<h2>Plural entries in a context</h2>
<pre><code>msgctxt "inbox"
msgid "%d message"
msgid_plural "%d messages"
msgstr[0] "%d bericht"
msgstr[1] "%d berichten"</code></pre>
<pre><code>label := tr.Ctl(loc, "navigation", "Home")
word := tr.Ctn(loc, "inbox", "message", "messages", count)</code></pre>
<h2>Legacy prefixes</h2>
<p>The default prefix separator is <code>__.</code>. The translator removes everything up to the last occurrence of that separator in translated output. <code>SetPrefixSeparator</code> changes it before use. This is output processing, not a replacement for a gettext <code>msgctxt</code> entry.</p>
<pre><code>tr.SetPrefixSeparator("__.")</code></pre>
<p>Prefer <code>ctl</code> and <code>ctn</code> for new contextual keys. Only choose a legacy separator that cannot appear unintentionally in the text you want to display.</p>
</article>
